    "28": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching vision",
          "heading": "Jake White dreams of Fiji hosting Ireland in Suva one day",
          "body": "White, speaking before the match, said there would be nothing greater than Fiji hosting Ireland in Suva, and he plans to move to Fiji in early 2027 to coach schools and clubs as well as the national side. The Aviva result went Ireland's way: Fiji lost 15-43, with a 26-0 second-half response settling a contest that was only 17-15 at the break. He credits timing for landing the job: \"I believe everything in life is timing.\""
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales stun All Blacks for first win since 1953",
          "body": "France beat South Africa 21-19."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "The42"
      }
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Centre spotlight",
          "heading": "Max Ojomoh shines at inside centre as England rout Japan 78-15",
          "body": "Planet Rugby's takeaways from Saturday's 78-15 win over Japan single out Max Ojomoh, who starred at inside centre, and the first minute backs them up: he threw the miss-pass that sent Will Joseph away for the opener. Japan were a man short from the start, Harry Hockings having been sent off for a dangerous hit on Ellis Genge, and England were 42 points clear by the half-hour. Henry Pollock, who had fancied the 14 shirt, is rumoured to be fuming, with Joseph wearing it after Immanuel Feyi-Waboso's injury ended his tournament."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales stun All Blacks for first win since 1953",
          "body": "France beat South Africa 21-19. Ireland beat Fiji 43-15."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Player praise",
          "heading": "Antoine Dupont hailed by press after France's 21-19 win over South Africa",
          "body": "Friday's 21-19 win over South Africa at the Stade de France is still generating praise for Antoine Dupont, who wore the No. 10 shirt. Planete Rugby's review, quoted in Midi Olympique's international press round-up, says he was decisive in two of the three tries and ran the game with magisterial control. Midi Olympique's James While called it one of the greatest individual performances he has covered in a test match. The review argues Dupont has largely undermined the arguments raised against him."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales stun All Blacks for first win since 1953",
          "body": "Ireland beat Fiji 43-15."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Rugbyrama"
      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Result reaction",
          "heading": "Tommy O'Brien and Baloucoune score braces as Ireland beat Fiji 43-15",
          "body": "Ireland are four wins from five in the Nations Championship, but ESPN's report judged the performance flattered to deceive despite the braces. Fiji had been heavily beaten by France in Lyon the week before, and new coach Jake White, who took the job last month, was still bedding in his side. Farrell's men now turn to South Africa, which The42 casts as Ireland's true final of the window, after a 42-12 win over Argentina the previous weekend."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales stun All Blacks for first win since 1953",
          "body": "France beat South Africa 21-19."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Aviva Stadium, Dublin"
      }
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Post-match view",
          "heading": "Argentina coach Contepomi says Italy dominated first half but failed to finish",
          "body": "Argentina coach Felipe Contepomi, speaking after the 19-14 win in Genoa, conceded that Italy had controlled possession and territory in the first half. His point was that in matches like this, the side that converts pressure into points wins, and Italy's problem was finishing. Captain Pablo Matera joined him at the press conference. Contepomi also said the Pumas kept their composure after playing a stretch with 13 men, calling his squad a team still under construction. Argentina next face France in Paris."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales stun All Blacks for first win since 1953",
          "body": "France beat South Africa 21-19. Ireland beat Fiji 43-15."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Stadio Luigi Ferraris, Genoa"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "OnRugby"
      }
    },
    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Captain's response",
          "heading": "Tuipulotu admits Scotland let themselves down in New Zealand defeat",
          "body": "Scotland captain Sione Tuipulotu, born and raised in Melbourne, says the squad have confronted their 21-43 defeat by New Zealand. \"It is always hard to watch the footage back after a defeat like that where we missed some big opportunities and let ourselves down in certain areas,\" he said. Tuipulotu expects Australia to arrive wounded after their 45-22 defeat by England at Twickenham, and says he will always carry extra fire against the Wallabies."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales stun All Blacks for first win since 1953",
          "body": "France beat South Africa 21-19. Ireland beat Fiji 43-15."
        }
      ],
