      }
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Post-match reaction",
          "heading": "Felipe Contepomi credits Pumas' character after grinding out 19-14 win in Genoa",
          "body": "Felipe Contepomi said the 19-14 win over Italy in Genoa owed more to character than control. Italy had dominated possession and territory in the first half, the Argentina coach acknowledged, and the final 20 minutes were very complicated as the Pumas finished with 13 men after yellow cards. Contepomi said the squad had stayed connected and found a way to win, and that Argentina have a good base to build on. He described a team still under construction, with two weeks together ahead of the trip to France."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales stun All Blacks for first win since 1953",
          "body": "France beat South Africa 21-19. Ireland beat Fiji 43-15."
