          "heading": "Dave Rennie admits All Blacks were 'one-dimensional' in 35-28 Wales defeat",
          "body": "Rennie admitted the All Blacks 'got a bit one-dimensional' as Wales won 35-28 in Cardiff, their first win over New Zealand since 1953. He pointed to the errors rather than the scoreboard: nine turnovers in the first half, four of them from offloads, and three attempts held up over the line in the second. Rennie said the review would cover selection and substitutions as well as the team's decision-making, and that the squad expects more of itself."
